5,"Mixe, Coatlán Language (MCO) – L1 & L2 Speakers, Status, Map ...",https://www.ethnologue.com/language/mco/,"Coatlán Mixe is a stable indigenous language of Mexico. It belongs to the Mixe-Zoquean language family. Direct evidence is lacking, but the language is thought to be used as a first language by all in the ethnic community. It is not known to be taught in schools.","Mixe, Coatlán",Mixe-Zoquean
6,"Mixe, Coatlan language. Evangelism tools, church planting ...",https://globalrecordings.net/en/language/mco,"Short audio Bible stories and evangelistic messages that explain salvation and give basic Christian teaching. Each program is a customised and culturally relevant selection of scripts, and may include songs and music. Audio-visual Bible lessons in 40 sections with pictures.","Mixe, Coatlán",Mixe-Zoquean
7,"Banda Filarmónica Municipal de Coatlán Mixe - FacebookMixe, Coatlán - worldmission.mediaMixe-Zoquean Voices -Mixe, Coatlán Language (MCO) – L1 & L2 Speakers, Status, Map ...",https://www.facebook.com/BandaMixeCoatlan/,"Aug 16, 2025 · Mixe is in Santa María Alotepec, Mexico. Banda Filarmónica Municipal de Coatlán Mixe. 1,187 likes · 1 talking about this. Música/Banda Mixe ""Tza'ny Ytu Am"" Mar 21, 2025 · Coatlán Mixe, spoken by around 5,000 people in Oaxaca, Mexico, is part of the Mixe-Zoque family. It plays a crucial role in preserving the cultural identity of the Coatlán community. Mixe-Zoquean Voices edited by Kondić, Ana & Gray, Russell is licensed under a Creative Commons Attribution Non Commercial 4.0. Coatlán Mixe is a stable indigenous language of Mexico. It belongs to the Mixe-Zoquean language family. Direct evidence is lacking, but the language is thought to be used as a first language by all in the ethnic community. It is not known to be taught in schools.","Mixe, Coatlán",Mixe-Zoquean
